{"user": "how could i have played differently?", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T01:15:08.296704+00:00", "assistant": "From the final board, the big issue is clear: **White got 3 corners** \u2014 a1, h1, a8 \u2014 and most of the top/left/bottom edges became permanent White discs. Black only got h8.\n\nSo the main \u201cdifferent play\u201d was:\n\n- **Don\u2019t focus on flipping many discs immediately.**\n- **Avoid giving White access to empty corners**, especially moves next to corners like **g2 near h1** or edge moves near **a8** unless you\u2019ve counted the sequence.\n- In the endgame, look for moves that **leave White with few/no legal replies** or force White to give you the corner.\n\nA useful question each turn would have been:  \n**\u201cAfter my move, can White take a corner or stable edge?\u201d**  \nIf yes, it\u2019s usually bad even if your move flips a lot.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T01:15:18.452965+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T01:15:21.223719+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Prompt": 1, "Local Justification": 2, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Prompt": 0.3333333333333333, "Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Prompt"], "llama": ["Boa